    "created_at": "2016-12-15T21:10:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-12-15T21:10:43Z",
    "body": "It also makes the `close()` method a no-op while the element has no `open` attribute. I understand that this is implemented in Chromium, but it's just one shipped implementation? We're not constrained by Web compat here, are we?\r\n\r\nIf implementors are happy with this, then fine. It just seems a bit broken to me.",
